# Kal backend — local development environment.
# Copy to .env and adjust. NEVER commit .env (real credentials live only there).
#
# Local dev database: an empty `kal` database on the machine's local PostgreSQL.
# Schema reaches it ONLY through reviewed migrations (see README "Database
# migrations") — never `prisma db push`.
#
# Connection-role convention (README "Roles & row-level security"):
# DATABASE_URL connects as your admin/migration user (it runs migrations and
# may create the cluster-level roles). Request-scope data access runs as the
# NOLOGIN role `kal_app` via `SET ROLE` per transaction — not via this URL.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/kal?schema=public"
